---
id: org.dxos.plugin.library
name: LibraryPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Library is a personal reading list built on ECHO. A book has a public, catalog-eligible face
(title, authors, reading status, rating, review, genres) and a private face that never leaves the
space (notes, ownership, personal tags). The public face maps to a `buzz.bookhive.book` atproto
record so the generic atproto companion can publish it to the user's PDS.

## Extensions

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`        |
| `flow`      | `org.dxos.mdl.flow@1.0`        |
| `step`      | `org.dxos.mdl.step@1.0`        |

## Types

```mdl
type Book
  desc: A book in the reading list. Public fields map to buzz.bookhive.book; private fields are ECHO-only.
  fields:
    title: string                                   # public
    authors: string[]                               # public
    status?: finished | reading | wantToRead | abandoned   # public
    stars?: number                                  # public, 1..10
    review?: string                                 # public
    startedAt?: string                              # public
    finishedAt?: string                             # public
    genres: string[]                                # public
    hiveId?: string                                 # public, BookHive catalog id
    hiveBookUri?: string                            # public
    coverUrl?: string                               # public
    notes?: string                                  # private
    owned?: boolean                                 # private
    format?: string                                 # private
    purchasePrice?: number                          # private
    purchaseDate?: string                           # private
    shelfLocation?: string                          # private
    personalTags: string[]                          # private
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Reading list CRUD in the content group
  req F-1.1: The Book type appears as a section in the navigation tree's content group.
  req F-1.2: A book can be created, renamed, opened as a full-page editable form, and deleted.
  req F-1.3: Collection tiles render a card body (cover, authors, status, rating).

feat F-2: BookHive-backed create autocomplete
  req F-2.1: The create form offers a type-ahead over the public buzz.bookhive.searchBooks endpoint.
  req F-2.2: Selecting a result autofills title, authors, coverUrl, genres, hiveId, hiveBookUri.

feat F-3: Publishable public face
  req F-3.1: The Book type carries an AtprotoRecordAnnotation (buzz.bookhive.book + generated codec).
  req F-3.2: Only fields marked publish via AtprotoVisibilityAnnotation are eligible to publish; mirror fields resolve from the upstream catalog; all others are private.
  req F-3.3: The codec provably never emits private fields (notes, ownership, personal tags).
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
test T-1: Create a book via autocomplete
  given: a space with the library plugin enabled
  when: the user searches "dune" and selects a result
  then: a Book is created with title, authors, coverUrl, genres, and hiveId populated

test T-2: Private fields never publish
  given: a Book with notes, owned, and personalTags set
  when: the codec encodes the book to a buzz.bookhive.book record
  then: the encoded record contains no notes, ownership, or personalTags data
```

## QA

Executable flows. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by flow and step number.

plugin-library has no `## Operations` section and no `key:`-bearing runtime operations in
`src/` — creation goes through a plain object-creation capability
(`capabilities/create-object.ts`), and `atproto/bookhive.ts`/`http.ts` are internal HTTP helpers,
not invocable ops. plugin-library is dev-only in `getDefaults` (`isDev`), so OFF by default for a
normal user.

```mdl
flow QA-1: Create a book via BookHive autocomplete, then delete it
  desc: The core library round-trip — search the public catalog, create a Book from a result, see
    it rendered, then remove it.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-2.1, F-2.2]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - collection: a collection in that space, to create into
    - plugin-library is enabled — it is OFF by default (isDev-only default). Enabling is a UI
      action (Settings -> plugin registry).
    - no Book titled "Dune" exists in the space — ABORT rather than deleting one this flow did not create
    - book: the Book "Dune" this flow creates — no create op exists (human-only step), so the
      runner binds this once that step completes
  test:
    - name: Search and create from a BookHive result
      do: In the navtree, click + on a collection and choose Book. Type "dune" into the create
        form's type-ahead and select the "Dune" result.
      expect: a Book appears under the collection, titled "Dune", with authors, cover, genres and
        hiveId autofilled from the BookHive result
      note: |
        NO `invoke` — no create operation exists for Book (only a UI factory capability); the
        BookHive search itself is a live public-API call (buzz.bookhive.searchBooks) with no local
        fixture, so this step is human-only end to end.
    - name: Open it as a full-page form
      do: Click "Dune" in the navtree.
      expect: an editable form opens showing title, authors, status, rating, review, and genres
  after:
    - name: Delete the book
      do: Right-click "Dune" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$given.book], target: $given.collection }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree
```
